{"name":"Gigas","hex":"#564786","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Giants (Greek mythology)","blocks":[{"text":"In Greek and Roman mythology, the Giants, also called Gigantes, were a race of great strength and aggression, though not necessarily of great size, known for the Gigantomachy, their battle with the Olympian gods. According to Hesiod, the Giants were the offspring of Gaia (Earth), born from the blood that fell when Uranus (Sky) was castrated by his Titan son Cronus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Poseidon_Polybotes_Cdm_Paris_573.jpg/330px-Poseidon_Polybotes_Cdm_Paris_573.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giants_(Greek_mythology)","wikidata":"Q191192"},{"title":"Gigas (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Gigas is an international cloud computing services company based in Madrid, Spain. The company began as a start-up in 2011.\nThe company has data centers in Madrid and Miami, and offices in Spain, US, Colombia, Chile, Peru and Panama."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Gigas_logo.png/330px-Gigas_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gigas_(company)","wikidata":"Q17054308"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Athena_Enkelados_Louvre_CA3662.jpg/500px-Athena_Enkelados_Louvre_CA3662.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Athena_Enkelados_Louvre_CA3662.jpg/1280px-Athena_Enkelados_Louvre_CA3662.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Athena_Enkelados_Louvre_CA3662.jpg/500px-Athena_Enkelados_Louvre_CA3662.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail",